  "publication_day": "2026-07-03",
  "article_opening": "By Ben Wodecki\nAMS-Osram, an Austrian semiconductor manufacturer of light and sensor solutions, poached a networking director from Nvidia.\nAshkan Seyedi had served as Nvidia’s lead for technical product marketing on its co-packaged and pluggable interconnect solutions since 2021. In a LinkedIn post , Sayedi revealed he’s taking on the role of VP and GM of AMS-Osram’s optical interconnect business line.\nThe firm, whose headquarters is located on the grounds of an old Austrian castle in Premstätte",
  "passage": "By Ben Wodecki\nAMS-Osram, an Austrian semiconductor manufacturer of light and sensor solutions, poached a networking director from Nvidia.\nAshkan Seyedi had served as Nvidia’s lead for technical product marketing on its co-packaged and pluggable interconnect solutions since 2021. In a LinkedIn post , Sayedi revealed he’s taking on the role of VP and GM of AMS-Osram’s optical interconnect business line.\nThe firm, whose headquarters is located on the grounds of an old Austrian castle in Premstätten and just a short drive from the city of Graz, is looking to push into the data center space. Its core microLEDs and vertical-cavity surface-emitting laser (VCSEL) technologies are set to power photonic optical connections for AI data centers.\nAMS-Osram is initially targeting its photonic tech for short-distance connections between ser…",
